body:
FOI Team,

Thank you for your email concerning FOI:2026-036.

I do not agree that FOI:2026-032 should be closed or treated as replaced.

The three matters are distinct and should remain so.

Internal review of FOI 2026-024
This remains a review of how the original 27 July request was interpreted and searched. I confirm it is separate. Nothing in FOI:2026-036 is a comment on that review.

FOI 2026-032 (your letter of 26 August 2026; also written by you as FOI 2026-32) This is the request you yourselves extracted from my 26 August email. Its subject is the records your searches for FOI 2026-024 had already identified: the “other archaeological discoveries recorded at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough” and the Church Farm, Llandough finds which you excluded from 2026-024 as out of scope. You registered that as a new request and gave a response date of 23 September 2026. That request has not been withdrawn. Those records have already been located. They do not require a new collection-wide trawl.

FOI:2026-036 (my email of 8 September 2026). This is a new request. It is not a restatement of 2026-032. It has additional limbs:

a schedule of every object, archive file, accession, loan, enquiry or correspondence record indexed, provenanced or otherwise recorded as from Great House Farm / Ty Mawr / Llandough Farm;

the Church Farm schedule only so far as already retrieved in the 2026-024 search, and without a new full trawl;

predecessor accession, register, day-book, donations-book and correspondence searches for 1875–1915 (Cardiff Museum / Welsh Museum of Natural History / National Museum of Wales) for ironwork, armour, visor, lance, helmet, “armour from Llandough”, or a find from Great House / Llandough Farm;

object records for Llandough ironwork not labelled “visor” or “lance” but associated with the farmhouse floor or rear wing / dairy.

If it assists you administratively, I have no objection to a single letter that answers both 2026-032 and 2026-036, provided that:
a. FOI 2026-032 is not closed, withdrawn or treated as superseded;

b. the records already identified in the 2026-024 search are scheduled and disclosed as a discrete part of that letter, and that part is provided by the date you gave for 2026-032 (23 September 2026);

c. the additional limbs of 2026-036 remain live and are answered on the 2026-036 timescale;

d. the two requests are not aggregated so as to refuse either under section 12;
e. the internal review of FOI 2026-024 continues independently.

The purpose of 2026-036 was to obtain the records you had already found and set aside, together with the predecessor-register and full-site schedule work that 2026-024 did not cover. It was not an invitation to extinguish 2026-032 or to restart the clock on material already retrieved.

Please confirm that FOI 2026-032 remains open on the terms above.

Regards,

Sion Buckler
hywelapbuckler@gmail.com
